  "english_1914": {
   "text": "‘Some say that the fairest thing on the black earth is a host of horsemen, others of foot, others of ships; but I say that is fairest which is the object of one’s desire. And it is quite easy to make this plain to all; for Helen observing well the beauty of men judged the best to be that one who destroyed the whole glory of Troy, nor bethought herself at all of child or parents dear, but through love Cypris led her astray. [Verily the wills of mortals are easily bent when they are moved by vain thoughts.] And I now have called to mind Anactoria, far away, whose gracious step and radiant glance I would rather see than the chariots of the Lydians and the charge of accoutred knights. We know well that this cannot come to pass among men . . .’",
   "translator": "B. P. Grenfell and A. S. Hunt (1914), literal prose",
   "anchor": {
    "page": 40,
    "note": "13-34",
    "scan": "https://archive.org/download/oxyrhynchuspapyr10gren/oxyrhynchuspapyr10gren_jp2.zip/oxyrhynchuspapyr10gren_jp2%2Foxyrhynchuspapyr10gren_0064.jp2"
   },
   "bracketed": "[Verily the wills of mortals are easily bent when they are moved by vain thoughts.]",
   "bracket_meaning": "G&H's own brackets: their rendering of a conjectured restoration of lines 25-6"
  }
 },
 "sappho31": {
  "title": "Sappho 31 Voigt = Wharton 2 (Bergk 2), 'That man seems to me peer of gods'",
  "greek_lines": [
   {
    "n": 1,
    "text": "Φαίνεταί μοι κήνος ἴσος θέοισιν",
    "anchor": {
     "source": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/57390/pg57390-images.html#frag2",
     "fragment": 2,
     "line": 1
    }
   },
   {
    "n": 2,
    "text": "ἔμμεν ὤνηρ, ὄστις ἐναντίος τοι",
    "anchor": {
     "source": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/57390/pg57390-images.html#frag2",
     "fragment": 2,
     "line": 2
    }
   },
   {
    "n": 3,
    "text": "ἰζάνει, καὶ πλασίον ἆδυ φωνεύ-",
    "anchor": {
     "source": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/57390/pg57390-images.html#frag2",
     "fragment": 2,
     "line": 3
    }
   },
   {
    "n": 4,
    "text": "σας ὑπακούει",
    "anchor": {
     "source": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/57390/pg57390-images.html#frag2",
     "fragment": 2,
     "line": 4
    }
   },
   {
    "n": 5,
    "text": "καὶ γελαίσας ἰμερόεν, τό μοι μάν",
    "anchor": {
     "source": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/57390/pg57390-images.html#frag2",
     "fragment": 2,
     "line": 5
    }
   },
   {
    "n": 6,
    "text": "καρδίαν ἐν στήθεσιν ἐπτόασεν·",
    "anchor": {
     "source": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/57390/pg57390-images.html#frag2",
     "fragment": 2,
     "line": 6
    }
   },
   {
    "n": 7,
    "text": "ὡς γὰρ εὔιδον βροχέως σε, φώνας",
    "anchor": {
     "source": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/57390/pg57390-images.html#frag2",
     "fragment": 2,
     "line": 7
    }
   },
   {
    "n": 8,
    "text": "οὐδὲν ἔτ' εἴκει·",
    "anchor": {
     "source": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/57390/pg57390-images.html#frag2",
     "fragment": 2,
     "line": 8
    }
   },
   {
    "n": 9,
    "text": "ἀλλὰ κὰμ μὲν γλῶσσα ἔαγε, λέπτον δ'",
    "anchor": {
     "source": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/57390/pg57390-images.html#frag2",
     "fragment": 2,
     "line": 9
    }
   },
   {
    "n": 10,
    "text": "αὔτικα χρῷ πῦρ ὐπαδεδρόμακεν,",
    "anchor": {
     "source": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/57390/pg57390-images.html#frag2",
     "fragment": 2,
     "line": 10
    }
   },
   {
    "n": 11,
    "text": "ὀππάτεσσι δ' οὐδὲν ὄρημ', ἐπιρρόμ-",
    "anchor": {
     "source": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/57390/pg57390-images.html#frag2",
     "fragment": 2,
     "line": 11
